6-5ffb-45f2-aa3c-ab0587a3719a","uuid":"4815a922-6e0c-4d8c-bd40-03bb7a190814","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:44:08.981Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/product/product.yaml","content":"# Product document for `fix-loop-refine-feedback`.\n#\n# Its concepts cover every step of E2E-001, and the glossary defines\n# every term they declare but \"latency\"; the refined fix adds the entry\n# that defines it, shaped as the feedback asks.\n\ntitle: \"Fixture host project\"\n\ndescription:\n  summary: >-\n    A single MCP service, used by the true-bdd fixtures as the host\n    project a scenario registry describes.\n\nroles:\n  - name: Operator\n    definition: Runs the MCP service and watches what it answers.\n  - name: Client Developer\n    definition: Writes the clients that send the MCP service its requests.\n\nglossary:\n  - term: mcp service\n    means: >-\n      The service this project builds: it takes a message from a client\n      and answers it. What every Scenario of the project observes.\n  - term: reply\n    means: >-\n      What the MCP service sends back for one message, and how long it\n      took to arrive. A client waits on it, so its content and its delay\n      are both behaviour.\n\nconcepts:\n  given:\n    - concept: service running\n      means: The MCP service has started and accepts requests.\n      terms: [mcp service]\n  when:\n    - concept: message sent\n      means: A role sends a stated message to the MCP service, once.\n      terms: [mcp service]\n  then:\n    - concept: answer\n      means: The MCP service's reply to the message is exactly a stated text.\n      terms: [mcp service, reply]\n    - concept: reply time\n      means: The latency of the MCP service's reply to the message is at most a stated number of milliseconds.\n      terms: [mcp service, reply, latency]\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}}}
